Project Supporting Women’s Participation in Transboundary Flood Management in Nyiragongo Territory

**Location:** Nyiragongo Territory, North Kivu Province (DRC)\
**Period:** December 2025 – June 2026\
**Partners and funders:** GIZ, GOPA, ICGLR (International Conference on the Great Lakes Region)

In Nyiragongo Territory, transboundary floods affect thousands of families every year. Women, who are often at the forefront of ensuring household safety, access to water and family livelihoods, are rarely involved in flood prevention and disaster response decisions.

Carried out between December 2025 and June 2026 with the support of GIZ, GOPA and ICGLR, this project aims to strengthen women’s effective participation in transboundary flood management. It is built around several key areas:

- **Raising awareness** within communities of the importance of women’s role in flood risk management;
- **Building women’s capacities** in prevention, early warning and crisis response;
- **Promoting their inclusion** in local structures and decision-making mechanisms;
- **Encouraging cross-border cooperation** for more coordinated and sustainable risk management.

By placing women at the heart of action, the project helps build more resilient, inclusive communities that are better prepared to face the effects of flooding.
